{%- comment -%}
  PG RetroBox Buyer Photos (2026-09-26): the review pieces the R36S Pro page
  has and the RetroBox page did not, registered in
  templates/product.pg-retrobox.json only. The strip is
  sections/pg-ultra-shots.liquid (the R36S Ultra's port of the Pro story's
  strip) with pg-uls- renamed pg-rbp-, data-uls data-rbp, and the script
  pgx-pg-retrobox-shots.js.

  WHY. The RetroBox page was built on 2026-09-26 before the product had any
  reviews: its template set hide_reviews, and pg-retrobox-story left out the
  Pro story's buyer photo strip and its "Customer Reviews" title. The owner
  imported the RetroBox's reviews into Judge.me the same evening (30 of them,
  4.73 average; the feed's product_name reads "PocketEra RetroBox") and asked
  for the R36S page's format: "reviews show in breakdown at bottom and theres
  a verified reviews section at top of page. also theres a sliodehow of
  reviews near middle of page". hide_reviews is off in the template now, so
  pg-landing renders the rating line (pg-rev-link makes it "30 verified
  reviews" and a jump link), the rotating review card and the review grid
  with its histogram. This file adds the other two pieces, without rewriting
  the 31KB story section; the story's notes about them being left out are
  history now, and its lower() already seats the story above the grid.

  1. THE "CUSTOMER REVIEWS" TITLE over the grid: the Pro story's rules,
     restated. Printed whether or not the strip renders.
  2. THE BUYER PHOTO STRIP: every photo of every review Judge.me has synced
     for this product (judgeme.review_widget_data: the photo reviews first,
     then page one), one card per photo, each linking to the review grid.
     Nothing is invented: the stars, the name and the text are the review's
     own, and the pill over the rail prints the feed's own average and count,
     then follows the page's rating line once pg-rev-link has rendered it.
     The feed is shown as it comes (no allow list), and nothing renders while
     it holds fewer than three photos. Seated after the Add to cart button (a
     desktop) or the last tile, order 6 on phones, and looped, all exactly as
     on the Ultra (see the script).

  NOTE, as on the Pro and Ultra pages: the photos are served from
  ae-pic-a1.aliexpress-media.com, so these are imported supplier reviews, not
  reviews collected by this store.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* the reviews open with a real title, centred, and no rule across the page
     (pg-pro2-story's rules, as on the Pro and Ultra pages) */
  #pgx #pg-reviews{border-top:0;margin-top:8px;padding-top:34px}
  #pgx #pg-reviews:before{content:"Customer Reviews";display:block;margin:0 0 28px;text-align:center;
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:32px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#fff}
  @media (max-width:900px){
    #pgx #pg-reviews{margin-top:4px;padding-top:28px}
    #pgx #pg-reviews:before{font-size:26px;margin-bottom:22px}
  }
</style>
{%- assign jm = product.metafields.judgeme.review_widget_data.value -%}
{%- assign jm_all = '' | split: '' -%}
{%- if jm -%}
  {%- if jm.photo_gallery -%}{%- assign jm_all = jm_all | concat: jm.photo_gallery -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if jm.reviews -%}{%- assign jm_all = jm_all | concat: jm.reviews -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign shots = 0 -%}
{%- capture shots_html -%}
{%- assign seen2 = '|' -%}
{%- for r in jm_all -%}
{%- assign key2 = '|' | append: r.uuid | append: '|' -%}
{%- unless seen2 contains key2 -%}
{%- assign seen2 = seen2 | append: r.uuid | append: '|' -%}
{%- if r.body != blank -%}{%- assign r_text = r.body -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign r_text = r.body_html | strip_html | strip -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign r_stars = r.rating | plus: 0 -%}
{%- for pic in r.pictures_urls -%}
{%- assign pic_url = pic.huge | default: pic.original | default: pic.compact | default: pic.small -%}
{%- if pic_url != blank -%}
{%- assign shots = shots | plus: 1 -%}
<a class="pg-rbp-shot" href="#pg-reviews">
  <img src="{{ pic_url }}" alt="Customer photo from {{ r.reviewer_name | default: 'a verified buyer' | escape }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" width="400" height="500">
  <span class="pg-rbp-cap">
    <span class="st">{%- for s in (1..5) -%}{%- if s <= r_stars -%}&#9733;{%- else -%}&#9734;{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}</span>
    <span class="nm">{{ r.reviewer_name | default: 'Verified buyer' | escape }}</span>
    {%- if r_text != blank -%}<span class="tx">{{ r_text | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
  </span>
</a>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if shots > 2 -%}
{%- assign rbp_avg = jm.average_rating | times: 1.0 | round: 1 -%}
<style>
  /* the strip: the Pro page's rules, renamed. min-width:0 and overflow:hidden
     keep a horizontal scroller from widening the buy column (pg-page-polish
     does the same for the Pro's strip). */
  #pgx .pg-rbp-shots{margin:16px 0 4px;min-width:0;max-width:100%;overflow:hidden;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-shots-h{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:flex-end;gap:10px;margin:0 2px 9px}
  /* under the headline the caption keeps only its "Swipe" hint, right-aligned;
     the BUYER REVIEWS words read as a second title and are hidden */
  #pgx .pg-rbp-shots-h b{display:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-shots-h span{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#C79BEA;white-space:nowrap}
  /* the "loved by" header over the photo rail: our purple pill with the page's
     own rating and review count, the purple gradient second line. No invented
     customer counts. */
  #pgx .pg-rbp-loved{text-align:center;margin:30px 0 6px}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-loved-pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#7A2FA2,#9B4BC4 55%,#B478E0);color:#fff;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.02em;line-height:1;box-shadow:0 12px 26px -14px rgba(155,75,196,.9)}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-loved-pill .st{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.08em}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-loved h3{margin:12px 0 0;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:27px;line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#fff}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-loved h3 span{display:block;background:linear-gradient(100deg,#F3E8FF 0%,#D9B3F5 30%,#B06CE8 60%,#8B3FB8 100%);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent}
  /* the rail loops (the set is printed five times; the script keeps the rail on
     the middle copy). It does not scroll by itself. Cards are a fixed width:
     cqw is 46% of the rail where container units work, 44vw the fallback. */
  #pgx .pg-rbp-rail{overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;overscroll-behavior-x:contain;container-type:inline-size;
    scrollbar-width:none;-ms-overflow-style:none;margin:0 -2px;padding:0 2px 4px}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-rail::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-track,#pgx .pg-rbp-set{display:flex;gap:10px;width:max-content}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-shot{flex:0 0 auto;width:min(210px,44vw);width:min(210px,46cqw);display:block;text-decoration:none !important;
    background:#16101F;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;color:#F1EDF7}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-shot img{display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5;object-fit:cover;background:#0D0714}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-cap{padding:8px 10px 10px}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-cap .st{color:#C79BEA;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;line-height:1}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-cap .nm{display:block;margin-top:4px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
  #pgx .pg-rbp-cap .tx{margin:3px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.4;color:#CFC4DE;
    display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:3;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
  @media (max-width:900px){
    /* on a phone the buy column is a flex column: the strip follows the tiles'
       run (5) and leads the accordions (6), as on the Pro page */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-rbp-shots{order:6;margin:6px 0 18px}
  }
</style>
<div id="pg-rbp-shots-src" hidden>
  <div class="pg-rbp-shots" data-rbp="shots">
    <div class="pg-rbp-loved"><span class="pg-rbp-loved-pill"><span class="st" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span><span data-rbp-loved="pill">Rated {{ rbp_avg }}/5 &middot; {{ jm.number_of_reviews }} reviews</span></span><h3>Loved by Gamers<span>Just Like You</span></h3></div>
    <div class="pg-rbp-shots-h"><b>Buyer Reviews</b><span>Swipe &rarr;</span></div>
    {%- capture shots_clone -%}{{ shots_html | replace: '<a class="pg-rbp-shot"', '<a tabindex="-1" class="pg-rbp-shot"' }}{%- endcapture -%}
    <div class="pg-rbp-rail" data-rbp-loop><div class="pg-rbp-track"><div class="pg-rbp-set">{{ shots_html }}</div><div class="pg-rbp-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-rbp-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-rbp-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-rbp-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="{{ 'pgx-pg-retrobox-shots.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG RetroBox Buyer Photos", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG RetroBox Buyer Photos"}]}
{% endschema %}
